From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ramin Moussavi <lordrasmus@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:46:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] microblaze: do not take a TLS symbol plus a large offset as
 an address

microblaze_classify_address rejects a thread-local SYMBOL_REF, and in
the base + (const (plus sym offset)) form it rejects it as well, but only
when the offset is a SMALL_INT.  A bare (const (plus tls_sym offset))
with a larger offset reaches the CONST case, which accepts it as an
absolute address without looking at the symbol.  At -O2

  __thread unsigned char a[65536];
  int f (void) { return a[65535]; }

then loads from the link-time address of the TLS template:

  imm   1
  lbui  r3, r0, -1        ; R_MICROBLAZE_64 a+0xffff

instead of going through __tls_get_addr and R_MICROBLAZE_TLSDTPREL64.
Any constant offset above 32767 triggers it, for every TLS model,
without -fPIC.  In .tbss that faults; in .tdata it silently reads or
overwrites the initialization image instead of the thread's copy.

Reject TLS references in the CONST case too, so the address goes
through microblaze_legitimize_address.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/microblaze/microblaze.cc (microblaze_classify_address):
	Reject a CONST that refers to a TLS symbol.

Signed-off-by: Ramin Moussavi <lordrasmus@gmail.com>
---
 gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.cc | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.cc b/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.cc
index 84f40f9eedf9..2fe85032dca5 100644
--- a/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/microblaze/microblaze.cc
@@ -875,6 +875,10 @@ microblaze_classify_address (struct microblaze_address_info *info, rtx x,
 
 	if (GET_CODE (x) == CONST)
 	  {
+	    /* (const (plus tls_symbol offset)) is not an absolute address;
+	       it has to go through microblaze_legitimize_address.  */
+	    if (microblaze_tls_referenced_p (x))
+	      return false;
 	    if (GET_CODE (XEXP (x, 0)) == UNSPEC)
 	     {
 		info->regA = gen_raw_REG (mode,
-- 
2.53.0

